# Automatic Picture in Picture of a window out of sight asks the window server what is in front of
# the window once macOS calls it not visible. Chrome's page host window sits in front of the main
# window with its frame and alpha 0, and must count as the window's own part: on macOS 27.2.1 a
# window alone on a second display sent its video to Picture in Picture when another app became
# active on the first (GitHub #533). The readout reads the real list: the shown page's host window
# is in front, and it is the window's own.
# promise: #533
budget rss=700 stalls50=5

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=coverage
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1
wait 1
cra://debug?windowCoverage=1
expect-log window coverage: on screen, [0-9]+ in front \([1-9][0-9]* own parts, [1-9][0-9]* see-through\)
